3. Functional Requirements
3.1 Multi-Dataset Support
Objective

Allow users to upload and manage multiple datasets within a single report.

Functional Requirements

Users must be able to:

Upload multiple files.

View list of datasets.

Rename dataset.

Delete dataset.

Use fields from multiple datasets in charts.

Constraints:

All datasets must pass through transformation pipeline.

Each dataset maintains its own:

originalDataset

transformations

computedDataset

Dataset Model Structure
{
  "datasets": [
    {
      "id": "dataset_1",
      "name": "Sales",
      "originalDataset": {},
      "transformations": [],
      "computedDataset": {}
    }
  ]
}
Acceptance Criteria

Upload 2 datasets → both appear in dataset panel.

Fields selectable per dataset.

Deleting dataset removes dependent charts.

Dataset rename updates everywhere.

3.2 Relationship Builder
Objective

Enable users to define relationships between datasets.

Functional Requirements

User must be able to:

Open relationship builder UI.

Drag column from Dataset A → Dataset B.

Define:

One-to-many

Many-to-one

Delete relationship.

View relationship diagram.

Rules:

Only compatible data types allowed.

Warn if relationship creates circular dependency.

Support multiple relationships.

Relationship Structure
{
  "relationships": [
    {
      "fromDataset": "Sales",
      "fromColumn": "CustomerID",
      "toDataset": "Customers",
      "toColumn": "CustomerID",
      "type": "one-to-many"
    }
  ]
}
Backend Requirement

Build relational graph.

Maintain schema map.

Validate joins dynamically.

Prevent ambiguous joins.

Acceptance Criteria

Relationship correctly joins datasets.

Charts can use fields from both datasets.

Deleting relationship updates dependent charts.

Circular relationships blocked.

3.3 Semantic Data Model Layer
Objective

Create unified logical model from multiple datasets.

Requirements

System must:

Build model graph from datasets + relationships.

Resolve joins dynamically when chart query executed.

Support:

Inner join

Left join

Prevent ambiguous join paths.

Model Representation
{
  "model": {
    "tables": [],
    "relationships": []
  }
}
Query Engine Requirement

When user builds chart using fields from:

Sales.Revenue

Customers.Region

System must:

Detect relationship.

Build join plan.

Aggregate correctly.

Return grouped result.

Acceptance Criteria

Multi-table chart renders correctly.

Join respects relationship direction.

Removing relationship breaks dependent charts safely.

No incorrect aggregations.

3.4 Calculated Columns
Objective

Allow users to create row-level computed fields.

Functional Requirements

User must be able to:

Add calculated column to a dataset.

Enter formula.

Reference other columns in same dataset.

Edit/delete calculated column.

Example formulas:

Profit = Revenue - Cost

Margin = (Revenue - Cost) / Revenue

FullName = FirstName + " " + LastName

Rules:

Calculated columns evaluated per row.

Must validate syntax before saving.

Must handle null safely.

Calculated Column Structure
{
  "calculatedColumns": [
    {
      "datasetId": "Sales",
      "name": "Profit",
      "formula": "Revenue - Cost"
    }
  ]
}
Technical Requirements

Build expression parser.

Prevent SQL injection or arbitrary code execution.

Type inference required.

Recompute when dataset changes.

Acceptance Criteria

Valid formula creates column.

Invalid formula shows error.

Column available in chart dropdown.

Updates dynamically when base column changes.

3.5 Measures (Aggregation Engine)
Objective

Enable dynamic aggregation independent of row-level data.

Functional Requirements

User must be able to:

Create Measure.

Define formula using aggregation functions.

Use measure in any chart.

Edit/delete measure.

Supported functions (minimum):

SUM()

AVG()

COUNT()

MIN()

MAX()

DISTINCTCOUNT()

DIVIDE()

IF()

RANK()

Running total (basic)

Example:

TotalRevenue = SUM(Sales.Revenue)

ProfitMargin = DIVIDE(SUM(Profit), SUM(Revenue))

Measure Structure
{
  "measures": [
    {
      "name": "TotalRevenue",
      "formula": "SUM(Sales.Revenue)"
    }
  ]
}
Technical Requirements

Measures evaluated at query time.

Must respect:

Global filters

Cross filters

Chart filters

Drill state

Build aggregation execution engine.

Prevent circular measure dependency.

Validate syntax before saving.

Query Execution Flow

When rendering chart:

Apply dataset transformations.

Apply relationships.

Apply filters.

Apply grouping.

Compute measures.

Return aggregated dataset.

Acceptance Criteria

Measure computes correctly.

Works across related tables.

Updates with filters.

Circular reference blocked.

Performance acceptable for 50k rows.

3.6 Model Persistence & Validation
Objective

Ensure model stability and recoverability.

Requirements

System must persist:

Datasets

Relationships

Calculated columns

Measures

On reload:

Model must reconstruct correctly.

Dependent charts must validate.

Invalid measures flagged.

Validation Rules

No duplicate measure names.

No duplicate calculated column names.

No circular relationships.

No circular measure dependency.

No ambiguous join path.

4. Performance Requirements

Must support 50k rows per dataset.

Join operations optimized.

Aggregation engine efficient.

Query response < 500ms under typical load.

Avoid full recompute if only measure changes.

